ABSTRACTION_INDEX: 0.58  
DESCRIPTION: `bench/dm/_immune.py`, `check_dispatch_health()`: dispatch false-positive detection is non-idempotent across historical blocks because `_dispatch_blocks` and `_dispatch_successes_after_block` are never pruned or acknowledged, and the uniqueness key is only `dispatch_fp_{model_id}_{block_round}`. If a model is blocked repeatedly in the same round index across different runs/restarts or long-lived manager reuse patterns, historical residue can trigger stale diagnoses. More importantly within a single run, every old block remains re-scanned every round, making the check O(total historical blocks × successes). This is a correctness-through-performance issue inside the immune boundary.  
PROPOSED_FIX: Mark consumed block rounds as diagnosed and prune satisfied pairs after emission.

